   "kind": "flashcard",
   "shape": "hand-authored",
   "label": "f02-sequence-guard",
   "front": "How does the provider-event sequence guard work, and where does it fall short?",
   "back": "Each verification keeps a providerSequence high-water mark. An event below it is stored with appliedToWorkflow false and receivedOutOfOrder true; an equal or higher one overwrites the verification. Gaps: equal sequences re-apply, there is no row lock, no idempotency key, and the \"provider\" is a logged-in loan officer.",
   "observation": "read-derived",
   "aiTag": false
  },
